' The linear pre-execution cost estimate of one offered deploy.
' One linear analysis runs before execution. It estimates the full cost
' (COMMs plus introduction, transfer and trace bytes) for every signature
' lane and resource class, and it decides whether the estimate is complete
' (rules X1 to X8 and the on-chain payer condition). A complete estimate
' holds exactly its cost plus the fee (P1 acceptance step 2, DR-64). An
' incomplete estimate holds up to the signed limit (the P1 margin rule).
' Settlement charges the measured use directly, with no floor, under the
' guard of DR-65 item 5.
'
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-impl/linear-cost-estimate.md
' Palette: inputs = supply blue · resolver and analysis = process lilac ·
'   estimate = delta orange · holds and supply check = gate teal ·
'   execution = pool green · settlement = note green ·
'   charged user failure = note amber · rejection = red ·
'   decisions = control amber · design notes = indigo note
' The legend also defines every name and symbol that the labels use,
' so the diagram reads on its own.
' Render:  ./render.sh linear-cost-estimate.puml

@startuml linear-cost-estimate
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $ca_neutral
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #333333
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_control
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #333333
skinparam PartitionBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
title The linear pre-execution cost estimate of one offered deploy

start
partition "1 · Inputs (the producer and every validator)" {
  :signed offered envelope: term, signers,\nfunding sources, phloLimit and phloPrice; <<$ca_supply>>
  :adopted schedule with the weights <latex>w_k</latex>,\noffered URN map, consensus host-work limits,\nwallet snapshot at <latex>R_0</latex>; <<$ca_supply>>
}
partition "2 · Resolver" {
  :resolve the names of the deploy from the envelope seed\n(metered, linear, stack-safe)\nholes inside receive bodies (DR-121); <<$ca_process>>
}
partition "3 · One linear analysis, two outputs" {
  :give every level a binder kind:\nfresh, fresh hole, URN, injection,\nreceive pattern, match pattern; <<$ca_process>>
  :size every send and receive from representative values\n(data after evaluation, poison for received values)\nand fill the channel tables <latex>M</latex>, <latex>T</latex>, <latex>\mathrm{TR}</latex>; <<$ca_process>>
  :count COMMs and introduction, transfer and trace bytes\nfor every region of every participant:\n<latex>V(s,k)</latex>, with maxima at branches and joins as multisets; <<$ca_process>>
  :<latex>B = \sum_{s}\sum_{k} w_k\,u(s)\,V(s,k)</latex>; <<$ca_delta>>
  floating note right $ca_note_indigo
    **What the estimate cannot see:** stored contracts that
    the deploy triggers, data from stored state, persistent or
    recursive processes, *x, method calls in process position,
    peeks. Each makes the estimate incomplete, and the
    margin rule of P1 covers it.
  end note
  if (do rules X1 to X8 and the\non-chain payer condition hold?) then (yes)
    :output: the estimate is complete\nno dynamic logic can add cost; <<$ca_process>>
  else (no)
    :output: the estimate is incomplete\nthe margin rule of P1 covers the unseen cost; <<$ca_process>>
  endif
}
partition "4 · Holds and the supply check at R0" {
  if (<latex>B > \mathrm{phloLimit}</latex> ?) then (yes)
    :reject before execution\nno effect · no charge; <<$ca_rejectfill>>
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
  if (is the estimate complete?) then (yes)
    :hold <latex>H = B \cdot \mathrm{phloPrice} + 1</latex>\nmeter bound <latex>B</latex>, source Certificate\n(P1 acceptance step 2, DR-64); <<$ca_gate>>
  else (no)
    :hold <latex>H = \mathrm{phloLimit} \cdot \mathrm{phloPrice} + 1</latex>\nmeter bound phloLimit, source SignedLimit\n(P1 margin rule, DR-64); <<$ca_gate>>
  endif
  :place the known demand per lane and class on eligible sources,\nthen fill the remainder <latex>R = (\mathrm{phloLimit} - B) \cdot \mathrm{phloPrice}</latex>\nin canonical custody order (no remainder when complete); <<$ca_gate>>
  if (do the holds fit the balances,\nthe caps and the total exposure at <latex>R_0</latex> ?) then (no)
    :reject before execution: "insufficient phlogiston"\nno effect · no charge; <<$ca_rejectfill>>
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
}
partition "5 · Execution in a fresh offered runtime" {
  :execute the deploy under the meter bound; <<$ca_pool>>
  if (meter outcome?) then (within the bound)
  elseif (signed limit exhausted\n(incomplete estimate)) then
    :classified user failure (DR-113): roll back,\ncharge the billable work and the fee; <<$ca_note_amber>>
    stop
  elseif (total use above <latex>B</latex>\n(complete estimate)) then
    :certificate failure: an analyzer defect\nreject, no charge; <<$ca_rejectfill>>
    stop
  else (host-work limit)
    :platform failure\nreject, no charge; <<$ca_rejectfill>>
    stop
  endif
}
partition "6 · Settlement and the guard" {
  :select the debits for the measured use\ncapacity of each purse: its signed caps and\n<latex>\mathrm{balance}(p) - \sum_{j>i} \mathrm{hold}_j(p)</latex>; <<$ca_gate>>
  floating note right $ca_note_indigo
    **Several offers per block (G2):** the capacity cap applies
    on the success path and on the rollback path.
    **Installer purses (G3):** a short installer purse follows
    the interim rule B5, which rejects the triggering deploy
    with no charge.
  end note
  if (guard of DR-65 item 5 for every purse p that member i debits\nor that carries a later hold:\n<latex>\mathrm{balance}_{\mathrm{after}}(p) - \mathrm{debit}_i(p) \geq \sum_{j>i} \mathrm{hold}_j(p)</latex> ?) then (yes)
    :settle: charge the measured use plus the fee\nhold = debit · refund implicit · no settlement floor; <<$ca_note_green>>
  else (no)
    :charged user failure: roll back to the execution root,\npay the billable work and the fee from the restored balance; <<$ca_note_amber>>
  endif
}
stop

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<$ca_supply>| signed input and consensus inputs |
  |<$ca_process>| resolver and linear analysis |
  |<$ca_delta>| the estimate in phlo |
  |<$ca_gate>| holds, placement and the supply check |
  |<$ca_pool>| execution under the meter bound |
  |<$ca_note_green>| settlement |
  |<$ca_note_amber>| charged user failure |
  |<$ca_rejectfill>| rejection with no charge |
  |<$ca_control>| decision |
  |<$ca_note_indigo>| design note |

  |= name |= meaning |
  | P1 | the paper "Cost-Accounted Rho Calculus" by L. G. Meredith, publications revision 0bf7817 |
  | DR-n | decision record n: DR-64 (the funding check before execution), DR-65 (same-block offers that share a purse), DR-113 (exhaustion of the signed limit), DR-121 (names that a receive body creates) |
  | G2, G3 | several offered deploys in one block, and installer funding of a stored continuation |
  | B5 | the interim rule of 2026-10-10 for an installer purse that cannot pay |
  | X1 to X8 | the completeness rules of the analysis |
  | COMM | the event in which a receive meets one datum for each of its binds |
  | URN | a uniform resource name that a new binds to a system channel |
  | *x | a dequotation, which runs the process that the name x quotes |
  | phloLimit, phloPrice | the signed phlo limit and the signed phlo price of the envelope |
  | <latex>R_0</latex> | the authenticated state root that the deploy funds from |
  | <latex>s</latex>, <latex>k</latex> | a signature lane, and a resource class: compute, introduction, transfer or trace |
  | <latex>V(s,k)</latex> | the raw count of lane s and class k, without units |
  | <latex>w_k</latex>, <latex>u(s)</latex> | the weight of class k, and the units of lane s |
  | <latex>M</latex>, <latex>T</latex>, <latex>\mathrm{TR}</latex> | the channel tables: largest datum message, largest transfer and largest trace on a channel |
  | <latex>B</latex> | the estimate in phlo |
  | <latex>H</latex>, <latex>R</latex> | the total hold, and the remainder of an incomplete estimate |
  | Certificate, SignedLimit | the bound sources of the meter: the estimate, or the signed limit |
  | <latex>p</latex>, <latex>i</latex>, <latex>j</latex> | a purse, the member that settles, and a later member of the same block |
  | <latex>\mathrm{hold}_j(p)</latex> | the hold of member j on purse p |
  | <latex>\mathrm{debit}_i(p)</latex> | the debit of member i on purse p, with the fee included |
  | <latex>\mathrm{balance}_{\mathrm{after}}(p)</latex> | the balance of p at the settlement root of member i |
  | <latex>\mathrm{balance}(p)</latex> | the balance of p that the selection reads |
endlegend

@enduml
